          "id": "http_errors",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "HTTP errors by service and class",
          "description": "4xx/5xx only — a per-2xx series would be a request-rate metric the logs already provide. The events-pipeline is absent by design: it is a Lambda with no HTTP surface. Tracking's 5xx are captured through an explicit exception branch, because Starlette's ServerErrorMiddleware sits outside every add_middleware layer and its 500 never reaches a send wrapper (docs/lessons/2026-08-12-server-error-middleware-outside-pure-asgi-middleware.md).",
